1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,013
What if every lie left a visible thread?

2
00:00:03,053 --> 00:00:05,746
A kid says, I didn't touch the cookies,

3
00:00:05,786 --> 00:00:08,479
and a bright red thread shoots from his

4
00:00:08,519 --> 00:00:10,791
mouth straight to the cookie jar.

5
00:00:10,831 --> 00:00:11,281
Busted.

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,927
Suddenly, a first date turns into a spider web.

7
00:00:15,967 --> 00:00:17,600
I love hiking, he says,

8
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,854
and a thread loops to his sofa.

9
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:21,963
She claims she's not nervous,

10
00:00:22,003 --> 00:00:24,653
and a thread ties to her shaking cup.

11
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,711
At the office it gets worse.

12
00:00:27,751 --> 00:00:30,156
Great idea, boss, says every employee,

13
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:32,729
and fifty red threads pile up around the

14
00:00:32,769 --> 00:00:36,267
meeting table like a very cranky cat's yarn collection.

15
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,039
Politicians struggle most.

16
00:00:39,079 --> 00:00:41,107
Their threads shoot into the sky,

17
00:00:41,147 --> 00:00:42,548
tangle with each other,

18
00:00:42,588 --> 00:00:45,430
and form a giant red knot above the town hall.

19
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:48,124
People begin to bring scissors to speeches.

20
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,074
Honestly, a world with visible lies might sound

21
00:00:52,114 --> 00:00:53,073
like a nightmare.

22
00:00:53,113 --> 00:00:54,661
In this thought experiment,

23
00:00:54,701 --> 00:00:57,659
it just forces everyone to try something different:

24
00:00:57,699 --> 00:00:58,953
tell the truth gently.

25
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:01,210
Here is the twist.

26
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,044
White lies leave pink threads,

27
00:01:03,084 --> 00:01:03,838
thin as hair.

28
00:01:03,878 --> 00:01:06,283
Your sweater's lovely, says your cousin,

29
00:01:06,323 --> 00:01:08,727
and the pink thread curls like a ribbon.

30
00:01:08,767 --> 00:01:11,539
Everyone starts wearing their ribbons proudly.

31
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:13,480
Years pass.

32
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,915
People learn that honesty isn't cruelty,

33
00:01:15,955 --> 00:01:17,437
and kindness isn't lying.

34
00:01:17,477 --> 00:01:19,628
The sky fills with threads at first,

35
00:01:19,668 --> 00:01:22,550
then slowly fewer, until one quiet morning there

36
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:23,524
are almost none.

37
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:26,339
At last, a child says,

38
00:01:26,379 --> 00:01:29,375
I love you, and no thread appears at all.

39
00:01:29,415 --> 00:01:30,781
Just a little glow.

40
00:01:30,821 --> 00:01:32,484
The whole street stops,

41
00:01:32,524 --> 00:01:34,187
looks up, and for once,

42
00:01:34,227 --> 00:01:36,853
the sky is perfectly clear and true.
